---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Pigeon from "../../assets/bpPigeon.png";
---

<Layout>
    <h1><strong><em>PIGEON!</em></strong></h1>
    <br />
    <br />
    <p>
        If you haven't noticed already, I kinda like pigeons. This is a page
        about pigeons. While you are learing about the best bird, try and find
        all 20 hidden pigeons, you'll get a very secret achievement if you do!
        <br />
        <br />
        Look, theres one right there!
    </p>
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="1" />
    <img
        src={Pigeon.src}
        class="pigeon"
        data-id="2"
        style="top: 45px; left: 0px;"
    />
    <img
        src={Pigeon.src}
        class="pigeon"
        data-id="3"
        style="top:460px; left: 75%; transform: scale(0.5)"
    />
    <img
        src={Pigeon.src}
        class="pigeon"
        data-id="4"
        style="top:160px; left:37%; width: 500px; height: 20px; filter:contrast(50%)"
    />
    <img
        src={Pigeon.src}
        class="pigeon"
        data-id="5"
        style="border-radius:100px; top:19px; left:58.6%; transform:scale(0.35)"
    />
    <img
        src={Pigeon.src}
        class="pigeon"
        data-id="6"
        style="filter:blur(3px); top:10px;"
    />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="7" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="8" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="9" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="10" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="11" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="12" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="13" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="14" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="15" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="16" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="17" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="18" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="19" style="position: ;" />
    <img src={Pigeon.src} class="pigeon" data-id="20" style="position: ;" />
    <br /><br /><br />
    <p>
        Oh and I know very little actual information about pigeons and I'm way
        too egotistical to google anything. Enjoy!<br /><br />
        So pigeons are actually one of the best animals. This is because they are
        actually quite intelligent have very few tasks in life. Pigeons are just cute
        little bystanders to life. They have very few motives for murder and enjoy
        driving buses.<br /><br />
        Pigeons probably live to around 15 years old based on the vibes they give
        off. Due to the almost domestication of the species has lead them to live
        shorter but happier lives. Most die to natural causes from the city air they
        breathe in and the significant lack of major predators. Pigeons also commonly
        die from an issue commonly called 'string foot' which occurs when a poor little
        pigeon gets their feet stuck in string, hair or some other material on the
        ground. This then tangles around their foot and can stop walking, cause deformities
        and restrict blood flow depending on severity. The only way to stop this is
        to keep city streets clean and if you see a pigeon with string foot to save
        it by removing the material around it's foot.<br /><br />
        Pigeon's main habitat has become cities and related areas. This is so they
        can get the attention they deserve. But this comes with the large downside
        of humans. Unfortuanetely not everyone understands how cool pigeons are and/or
        are extremely jealous of how cool they are. This means they face discrimination
        daily. People abuse them every hour of the day and no one bats an eye. Luckily
        living in cities comes with major upsides that out-weigh the abusive behavour
        they have to deal with. One large upside is the amount of buses they are able
        to see drive past. It's very common knowledge that pigeons want to drive the
        bus but unfortuanetely huamns hate them and don't allow them to drive the
        bus. But the next best thing is being able to watch the busses drive past
        constantly. It is kinda cruel to show them their life's goal drive past every
        day but life is cruel I guess. <br /><br />
        Some people say pigeons are secretely government spy robots but they actually
        aren't. The idea that pigeons are robots came from the misconception that
        baby pigeons don't exist, but they actually do cause pigeons aren't robots.
        The proof that pigeons aren't robot lies in the fact that if the government
        did make them, they would be dumb and ungly. And therefore chickens are government
        spy robots because they don't act like birds and look dumb. Chickens are dumb
        birds. The government tried to hide this by gaslighting people into thinking
        they are made of chicken. But the meat commonly called chicken is actually
        pork that the government has injected with tiny robots that can control your
        mind. The government uses these robots to make you beleive that chickens are
        birds. I haven't eaten government pork in years, they've lost control of me.
        IM FREE. <strong>IM FREE. </strong><strong><em>IM FREE!</em></strong>
    </p>
    <div id="counter">Pigeons found: 0 / 20!</div>
</Layout>
<script>
    const found = new Set(
        JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("foundPigeons") || "[]"),
    );

    const counter = document.getElementById("counter");

    function updateCounter() {
        counter.textContent = `Pigeons found: ${found.size} /20!`;

        if (found.size === 1) {
            window.unlockAchievement?.("ONE_PIGEON");
        }

        if (found.size === 10) {
            window.unlockAchievement?.("TEN_PIGEONS");
        }

        if (found.size === 20) {
            window.unlockAchievement?.("ALL_PIGEONS");
        }
    }

    document.querySelectorAll(".pigeon").forEach((pigeon) => {
        const id = pigeon.dataset.id;

        if (found.has(id)) {
            pigeon.classList.add("found");
        }

        pigeon.addEventListener("click", () => {
            if (found.has(id)) return;

            found.add(id);
            pigeon.classList.add("found");

            localStorage.setItem("foundPigeons", JSON.stringify([...found]));

            updateCounter();
        });
    });

    updateCounter();
</script>
